  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Friday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Cut off low ejects east along the \nnorthern Nevada border today with the associated weak frontal\nboundary moving thru northern Nevada from the west. West-\nnorthwesterly breezes will be present today, though winds will be more\nmodest than yesterday with gusts remaining less than 30 mph. Light\nrain showers and isolated thunderstorms can be expected along the\nIdaho and Oregon borders as well as the Utah border thru this\nevening. Any rain accumulations will be around 0.10 inches or\nless and the best opportunity for accumulating rainfall will be\nacross northern Elko County. Will maintain a low chance of light \nrain showers and isolated thunderstorms into Saturday for the far\nnortheast portion of Elko County, but generally speaking, weather\nwill be fair thru the weekend. Daytime high temperatures today \nwill be several degrees cooler than yesterday. Temperatures will \nwarm thru the weekend with daytime highs returning to the mid 70s \nto mid 80s by Sunday.\n\nA low chance of rain will be present across central Nevada in the\nMonday and Tuesday time frame as a modest Pacific low moves into \ncentral California from the west. That said, latest numerical \nmodel solutions are not in agreement on the exact track of the \nlow, which will be the determining factor with regard to rain\npotential. Fair weather looks to be in place the latter half of \nthe week. \n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence exists for \nshowers and thunderstorms along the northern and eastern NV \nborders today, though confidence is moderate with regard to rain\naccumulation. Significant grid edits required within PoP grids to\nbetter represent rain shower and thunderstorm chances today and\nthis evening.",
